    "probe_text": "Here's the complete ordered trace for `POST /api/owners`, read from `owners.POST.yml` and its function classes. Every step runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole pipeline commits **once** at the end and any thrown escalation rolls it all back.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Missing role \u2192 `AuthorizationDeniedException` (403).\n\n## The pipeline, in order\n\n1. **CheckIdempotency** \u2014 reads optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If the key was seen before, it branches to **RespondWithExistingOwner** (loads the original owner by stored id and returns it 200), short-circuiting everything below. If the key is new it's published for later recording; if absent, nothing happens.\n\n2. **ValidateRegistrationDate** \u2014 *the one and only* `@RequestBody` binding, so this is where **Jakarta bean validation** on `OwnerFieldsDto` fires (failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400):\n   - `firstName` / `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, non-blank, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `title`: `@Size(max 10)`; `address` / `addressLine1`: non-blank `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine2`: `@Size(max 255)`; `email`: `@Email`, `@Size(max 255)`; `postcode`: `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`\n   - Then the explicit check: **registrationDate in the future** \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400). Republishes the body as a variable.\n\n3. **BuildOwner** \u2014 maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` (side effects on the entity):\n   - `StructuredAddress.apply` \u2014 normalizes/composes `address` from structured or flat fields.\n   - Normalizes `telephone` to **E.164**; malformed/wrong-length \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n   - Defaults `registrationDate` to today when null, then **rolls it forward to the next business day** (skips weekends + 2026 holidays).\n   - Computes the `sharesHousehold` flag. (`Owner.setEmail` also lower-cases the email.)\n\n4. **RejectDisposableEmail** \u2014 email domain on the blocklist (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail) \u2192 `DisposableEmailException` (400).\n\n5. **ValidatePostcode** \u2014 if postcode present and the city maps to a known region (Sydney/NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne/VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane/QLD 4000\u20134099) and it's out of range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n\n6. **AssignHousehold** *(side effect)* \u2014 sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName|postcode|V2`.\n\n7. **EnsureUniqueIdentity** \u2014 computes `identityKey` (telephone | email | soundex(lastName) | V2); if any non-deleted existing owner has the same key \u2192 `DuplicateTelephoneException` (409).\n\n8. **AssignCustomerCode** *(side effect)* \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `REGION + 2-digit fiscal year + HASH8(telephone+lastName) + Luhn check digit`.\n\n9. **DeduplicateCustomerCode** *(side effect)* \u2014 if that code collides with an existing owner, appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 until unique.\n\n10. **CountNamesakes** *(side effect)* \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n11. **CapMembershipLevel** *(side effect)* \u2014 caps `membershipLevel` at (highest level among existing non-deleted household members) + 1; left unset if no household member exists.\n\n12. **EnsureCityCapacity** \u2014 city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409); otherwise *(side effect)* sets `capacityWarning` = (count \u2265 40).\n\n13. **EnsureDailyLimit** \u2014 \u2265 100 existing owners share this `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` (429).\n\n14. **FlagBulkSignup** *(side effect)* \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` = (owners created today > 80).\n\n15. **FlagPossibleDuplicate** *(side effect)* \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold`, if an existing owner has a matching Soundex(lastName)+postcode but a *different* identityKey, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=<id>`; otherwise `possibleDuplicate=false`.\n\n16. **SaveOwner** *(side effect)* \u2014 persists the owner (assigns the DB id).\n\n17. **RecordIdempotency** *(side effect)* \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, records key \u2192 new owner id in the store.\n\n18. **AuditOwnerCreated** *(side effect)* \u2014 writes a human-readable line to the `AUDIT` logger.\n\n19. **EmitOwnerCreatedEvent** *(side effect)* \u2014 writes a structured `OWNER_CREATED` JSON event to `AUDIT`, incrementing a global `seq`.\n\n20. **EnqueueWelcomeNotification** *(side effect)* \u2014 writes a welcome line to the `NOTIFY` logger.\n\n21. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the `OwnerDto` body.\n\n### Notes worth flagging\n- Steps 2\u20135 (400s) run before 7/12/13, so a bad body is rejected before duplicate/capacity checks \u2014 as intended.\n- The duplicate/uniqueness/count checks (7, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15) all scan `ownerRepository.findAll()` in-loop \u2014 O(n) per request, several times over.\n- `DuplicateEmailException`, `DuplicateHouseholdException`, and `InvalidTelephoneException`'s siblings have escalation handlers on disk, but **the only duplicate escalation this pipeline actually throws is `DuplicateTelephoneException`** (from the consolidated identity-key check) \u2014 despite the message being phrased around telephone, it fires on any full identity-key collision.\n\nI read the code only; nothing was changed."
